+# Beneficiary document intake and staff review
+
+Phase 2 originally built on beneficiary authentication commit `ce3ddc5` and staff backend `050c389`. For version 4.0 (`42b4552`), use the consolidated mobile-v4 patch instead of the old ordered phase patches. Staff review URLs/role checks are preserved; the staff frontend reads the same BeneficiaryDocument records.
+
+## Setup
+
+Run `npm run prisma:generate` and `npm run prisma:migrate:deploy`. Migration `20261103000100_allow_beneficiary_document_uploads` makes uploaded_by nullable and adds uploaded_by_beneficiary. A database check requires exactly one uploader: a staff User, or the beneficiary who owns the document. Existing staff attribution is preserved; mobile never impersonates staff.
+
+Files remain private under UPLOAD_ROOT/beneficiary-documents (default: uploads/beneficiary-documents relative to the API working directory). Optional DOCUMENT_STORAGE_DIR overrides that document directory for isolated tests. Back up files and PostgreSQL together. Persistent shared storage, malware scanning, crash/orphan recovery, and retention/deletion jobs remain separate work. Never expose the directory as a public static route. Tests use fresh temporary directories and synthetic files.
+
+## API
+
+All paths below are relative to `/api/v1/mobile` and require a beneficiary bearer token. Ownership comes from the session.
+
+| Method | Path | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/beneficiaries/me/documents` | Own records, newest first, including review decisions and corrected versions. |
+| POST | `/beneficiaries/me/documents` | Multipart documentType and one file named file. Returns 201 for new files; identical content/category/account returns the existing record and its current status with 200. |
+| POST | `/beneficiaries/me/documents/:documentId/replacement` | Same fields. An owned REJECTED file can be corrected using its original category. Creates a SUBMITTED record and marks the original SUPERSEDED. Repeated identical corrections return the same record; conflicts return 409. |
+| GET | `/beneficiaries/me/documents/:documentId/content` | Owner-only attachment, private/no-store, nosniff. Other accounts receive 404. File-viewing UI is not part of this milestone. |
+
+Use FormData and let fetch generate the Content-Type boundary. The original mobile backend's raw-byte protocol is not accepted here. PDF/JPEG/PNG are allowed up to 5 MiB (shown as 5 MB). Type is detected from bytes. Multipart requests allow one file, one category field, and an optional documentName. UTF-8 filenames are decoded for both staff and mobile, with legacy-name fallback. Removed records are excluded from lists, downloads and duplicate matching. Corrections inherit the original Other requirement's name and reject conflicting names; the current mobile form still offers generic categories.
+
+Public fields: id, docType (lowercase), originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, createdAt, status, reviewNotes, reviewedAt, replacesDocumentId, canReplace. Mappings: SUBMITTED -> received, ACCEPTED -> accepted, REJECTED -> rejected, SUPERSEDED -> superseded. Paths, hashes, staff identities, and uploader IDs stay private. Notes are displayed exactly as entered; switching interface language does not invent a translation.
+
+Existing staff list/review routes remain `/api/v1/beneficiaries/:beneficiaryId/documents` and `POST /api/v1/beneficiaries/:beneficiaryId/documents/:documentId/review`. DSWD Staff and System Administrators can review; mobile tokens cannot review their own documents. Document acceptance does not approve enrollment or verify identity.
+
+An account row lock serializes mobile retries. The session is rechecked after file receipt inside the write transaction, so finishing an upload after logout cannot create a document. Duplicate/rejected/failed writes clean up the new file. Correction transitions reuse staff validation and conditionally update the old status to protect against concurrent staff decisions. This covers normal errors, not process-crash recovery.
+
+## Verify
+
+```powershell
+npm test
+npm run prisma:validate
+$env:RUN_MOBILE_DB_TESTS='1'
+$env:AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_PER_15_MINUTES='100'
+npm run test:mobile:integration
+npm run test:mobile:documents
+```
+
+The document suite checks invalid/oversized/spoofed input cleanup, exact downloads, ownership, staff review visibility, database uploader constraints, simultaneous retries/corrections, unchanged eligibility, and logout during a streamed upload. Fixtures/files are removed afterward. The mobile repository's `npm run test:shared` also exercises uploads and rejection/correction/acceptance through its actual API module.
+
+The form retains failed selections, locks the category during correction, shows status/notes, and marks the old document replaced only after server confirmation. English/Bisaya and native/web request construction have automated checks. Android file-provider behavior and a complete browser/native visual walkthrough remain unverified.
