+# Mobile compatibility with staff version 4.0
+
+Reconciled on November 9, 2026 with backend `42b4552` and frontend `f6dfcdf`. The mobile repository's consolidated `integrations/shared-backend/mobile-v4.patch` applies directly to this backend base and contains all four mobile phases. Do not also apply the older version-3 phase patches.
+
+The shared backend retains the upstream transaction-aware PostgreSQL adapter, deployment upload root, stricter physical-package requirements, alternative QR-or-biometric verification, document names, and staff document removal. The mobile pool-size setting remains available for the embedded development database. Existing private environment values and mobile QR signing secrets must be preserved.
+
+Mobile document lists and owner downloads exclude staff-removed records. Removed documents do not intercept upload retries. Corrections retain the original named Other requirement and reject a conflicting name. The shared multipart intake permits the category, optional document name, and one file; staff named-document uploads still work. The current mobile form offers generic categories; selecting individual named Other requirements remains later UI work.
+
+Use `npm ci`, `npm run prisma:generate`, and `npm run prisma:migrate:deploy`. First apply migrations and run checks on a separate development test database. Preserve existing account records, private configuration and uploaded files; do not reset or reseed an existing database. The eight upstream version-4 migrations add claim verification timestamps, package evidence, referrals, named documents, removal status, alternative verification, and a wider email-provider constraint. The three mobile migrations remain unchanged.
+
+Run `npm test`, `npm run prisma:validate`, and the mobile authentication/document database suites. Use `--test-concurrency=1` when running the two database suite files together against embedded Prisma. The mobile repository's `npm run test:shared` verifies the actual client, enrollment review, scheduling, QR issuance/reopening, staff verification, and session isolation. Physical assistance test events now require a package name, unit, and quantity before opening. QR_OR_BIOMETRIC accepts QR alone; QR_AND_BIOMETRIC still needs both checks. Neither QR step itself releases assistance or credits a wallet.
+
+The old November 7 local test pass is expired. Create a new distribution with a future session and package details for the pending manual facilitator test. Existing administrator/reviewer accounts and authenticator enrollment are preserved. Source updates do not import a teammate's database or connect to their hosted environment.
